{
  "schema": "collab.recipes-manifest/v1",
  "repository_version": "0.1.0",
  "context": "Each Dockerfile COPYs repository-relative paths: the build context is a tree in which the recipe sits at its `path`, together with every path of its `shared` list. `name` is the release identifier and names a stack, never a repository; which repository uses which recipe, and which engine, is organization data that the planner reads from the canon. `parent` names what the base is, passed as the build argument `build_arg`: `{recipe, version}` is a recipe of this manifest (its released image); `{component, recipe?, version}` is the image built from a recipe of another released component (its release index key, and its manifest entry when that tree holds several); `{pin}` is an image no recipe builds (an operating-system or third-party image), named by a neutral profile that the organization pins by digest in its own declaration. A recipe never carries a registry, tag or digest of any organization. `inputs` maps each plan-time build argument to the organization fact the planner resolves for it; a recipe never carries the value. `helpers` lists the stable neutral commands a recipe installs, by capability. `context_inputs` names what the builder places at the root of the context itself (the exact Collab release the resolver recipes install as their last layer), and `context` says what fills each name, with the shape of a container recipe's `version.json` `build.context` (`{name, kind: tree|artifact, component: <release index key>, version: <constraint>}`): the version the organization runs is chosen by the console from its adoption, never by the recipe; every other COPY source is a path of the release tree, inside the recipe's `path` or one of its `shared` paths.",
